2026-08-29T14:40Z claude note adversarial review found a real bug in action 5 as written. Degrading to the runtime default on a failed dtype load is unsafe here: SearchIndexBase.build stamps vectorEmbedderId from the provider identity BEFORE embedding, so a provider that changed precision mid-flight leaves the index labelled with a precision its vectors do not have — undetectable downstream, since quantisation does not change vector width and the identity string is the only check. Across sessions the stale label can later MATCH a genuinely quantised identity and mix two spaces silently. Fixed by removing the substitution: the precision is constant for the provider's life and an unloadable value throws, reaching noteEmbedFailure so the index degrades to keyword-only with a named reason — the same path a missing transformers package takes. Action 5's intent (do not take the server down) holds; its mechanism (fall back to default precision) does not, and that is the third premise correction on this ticket. Fork now 5dceeb1, 11 tests, 9 red on stock, 858 passed.
