      degradation clears the dtype as well, so a fallback cannot leave the index
      labelled with a precision its vectors do not have
- [x] An unloadable dtype degrades with a named message — to keyword-only, not
      to another precision. Proven against `fp16`, which throws; `q7`, this
      ticket's chosen example, does NOT throw and would have passed against an
      implementation with no degradation path at all
- [x] Documented with the measured ladder and no recommendation. The device
      sentence says what measurement supports — none is passed, and none is
